    "evidence_text": "PCNA functions as a molecular platform to trigger Cdt1 destruction and prevent re-replication\n\nIn Xenopus egg extracts, Cdt1 is destroyed on chromatin during DNA replication.\n\nMutation of the PCNA-interaction motif yields a stabilized Cdt1 protein that induces re-replication.\n\nZMYND11 links histone H3.3K36me3 to transcription elongation and tumour suppression\n\nRecognition of modified histones by \u2018reader\u2019 proteins plays a critical role in the regulation of chromatin.\n\nUbiquitin-dependent protein degradation.\n\nA growing number of cellular regulatory mechanisms are being linked to protein modification by the polypeptide ubiquitin.\n\nKey role of Ubc5 and lysine-63 polyubiquitination in viral activation of IRF3.\n\nThe activation of IRF3 also requires two ubiquitin-binding domains of NEMO.\n\nUbiquitination on nonlysine residues by a viral E3 ubiquitin ligase.\n\nUbiquitination controls a broad range of cellular functions.\n\nThe last step of the ubiquitination pathway is regulated by enzyme type 3 (E3) ubiquitin ligases.\n\nThis form of ubiquitination required a cysteine residue in the intracytoplasmic tail of MHC I molecules.\n\nThus, ubiquitination can occur on proteins lacking accessible lysines or an accessible N terminus.\n\nAcetylation of Histone H3 Lysine 56 Regulates Replication-Coupled Nucleosome Assembly\n\nATPase-Dependent Control of the Mms21 SUMO Ligase during DNA Repair\n\nModification of proteins by SUMO is essential for the maintenance of genome integrity.\n\nYet how the activity of the SUMO ligase is controlled remains unknown.\n\nDNA damage tolerance during eukaryotic replication is orchestrated by PCNA ubiquitination.\n\nFork reversal is driven in vitro by multiple enzymes, including the DNA translocase ZRANB3, shown to bind polyubiquitinated PCNA.\n\nHowever, whether this interaction promotes fork remodeling and template switching in vivo was unknown.\n\nTargeting these fork protection systems represents a promising strategy to potentiate cancer chemotherapy.\n\nThe anaphase promoting complex/cyclosome: a machine designed to destroy\n\nAttachment of the ubiquitin-related protein Urm1p to the antioxidant protein Ahp1p.\n\nUrm1p is a ubiquitin-related protein that serves as a posttranslational modification of other proteins.\n\nUrm1p conjugation has been implicated in the budding process and in nutrient sensing.",
